@startuml class-diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

abstract class BaseEntity {
  + id : string
  + createdAt : Date
  + updatedAt : Date
  + deletedAt : Date [0..1]
}

class Category {
  + name : string
  + slug : string
}

class Product {
  + name : string
  + slug : string
  + description : string
  + roastLevel : RoastLevel
  + isOrganic : boolean = false
  + isFairTrade : boolean = false
  + status : ProductStatus = DRAFT
  + tastingNotes : string [0..1]
  + origin : string
  + processingMethod : string
}

class ProductVariant {
  + sku : string
  + weight : Decimal
  + unit : ProductUnit
  + name : string
  + price : Decimal
  + discountType : DiscountType [0..1]
  + discountValue : Decimal [0..1]
  + quantity : number = 0
}

class ProductImage {
  + url : string
  + isPrimary : boolean = false
  + sortOrder : number = 0
}

class User {
  + clerkId : string
  + email : string
  + role : UserRole = USER
  + firstName : string
  + lastName : string
  + phoneNumber : string [0..1]
  + avatarUrl : string [0..1]
  + status : UserStatus = ACTIVE
}

enum RoastLevel <<enumeration>> {
  LIGHT
  MEDIUM
  DARK
}

enum ProductStatus <<enumeration>> {
  DRAFT
  ACTIVE
  INACTIVE
  ARCHIVED
}

enum ProductUnit <<enumeration>> {
  KG
  G
  ML
  L
}

enum DiscountType <<enumeration>> {
  PERCENT
  FIXED
}

enum UserRole <<enumeration>> {
  ADMIN
  USER
}

enum UserStatus <<enumeration>> {
  ACTIVE
  INACTIVE
}

note bottom of ProductVariant
  sku is unique.
end note

note bottom of User
  clerkId and email are unique.
end note

note bottom of Product
  name is unique.
end note

note bottom of Category
  name is unique.
end note

' ---------------------------------------------------------------
' Relationships
' ---------------------------------------------------------------

' Inheritance (Generalization): every class is-a BaseEntity.
BaseEntity <|-- Category
BaseEntity <|-- Product
BaseEntity <|-- ProductVariant
BaseEntity <|-- ProductImage
BaseEntity <|-- User

note right of BaseEntity
  Inheritance: every class is-a BaseEntity
  and takes its identity, timestamps and
  deleted marker from it. BaseEntity is
  abstract: it never exists on its own.
end note

' Association: Product -> Category, navigable one way.
Product "0..*" --> "1" Category
note on link
  Association, not aggregation: a category
  classifies products, a product is not part of it.
  Only a product knows its category, so the
  arrow points to Category.
  1: every product belongs to exactly one category.
  0..*: a category can have no products.
  A category that still has products cannot be
  deleted.
end note

' Composition: variants and images belong to one product.
Product "1" *-- "1..*" ProductVariant
note on link
  Composition: a variant belongs to exactly one
  product. It is created with the product, changed
  only through it, and never exists on its own.
  1..*: a product always has at least 1 variant.
end note

Product "1" *-- "2..6" ProductImage
note on link
  Composition: same reasons as variants.
  2..6: a product must have exactly 1 primary
  image and at least 1 gallery image, at most 6
  in total.
end note

note bottom of ProductImage
  Deleting a product archives it (status
  ARCHIVED). Its variants and images go with it:
  they exist only as parts of their product.
end note

note top of User
  User has no relationship to another class;
  it is identified by the external sign-in
  provider (clerkId).
  Enums are attribute types, so no line is
  drawn to them.
end note

@enduml
